    key_formulas: '• Monohybrid Phenotype Ratio (Bb × Bb): 3 Dominant : 1 Recessive\n• Monohybrid Genotype Ratio: 1 BB : 2 Bb : 1 bb\n• Dihybrid Phenotype Ratio: 9 : 3 : 3 : 1\n• Test Cross / Backcross Ratio: 1 : 1\n• Sex Determination: Female (XX), Male (XY)',
    pro_tips_95: 'WAEC Examiner Secret: In sex-linked inheritance (e.g. hemophilia, red-green color blindness), the recessive gene is carried strictly on the X-chromosome. Males cannot be carriers — they are either normal or affected!',
