    summary_60s: 'Symbiosis, mutualism, parasitism and environmental studies. Practical use of ecological equipment, population studies in specific habitats, environmental changes and the biological impacts of climate change. ECOLOGY Ecology is the branch of biology that deals with the study of in',
    key_formulas: '• Population Density: Total Population / Land Area (km² or m²)\n• Capture-Recapture Method (Lincoln Index): N = (M × C) / R\n• 10% Energy Transfer Law: Only ~10% of energy transfers to each successive trophic level\n• Food Chain: Producer (Plants) → 1° Consumer (Herbivore) → 2° Consumer (Carnivore) → Top Predator',
