    summary_60s: 'Auxins, gibberellins, cytokinins, ascorbic acids and ethylene. GROWTH IN HIGHER PLANTS AND GROWTH REGULATORS PLANT GROWTH Growth is a fundamental characteristic of living organisms. In plants, growth is defined as a permanent and irreversible increase in size and mass , resulting',
